    <main id="main-content" class="static-main">
      <article class="px-5 pt-12 pb-6 lg:px-8 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-16 max-w-[1600px] mx-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-brand-200 uppercase tracking-wide">Chapter 7</span>
          <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-500/30 to-transparent"></span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="section-title text-3xl tracking-tight leading-tight lg:text-5xl"><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">Cryptography</span> Basics</h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] lg:mt-4 lg:text-xl text-brand-200">Public and private keys explained</p>

        <section class="mt-8 lg:mt-12 reveal" id="introduction">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Introduction</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">Cryptography</span> is the science of writing secret codes. For thousands of years, humans have used ciphers and <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('encryption')">encryption</span> to protect messages from prying eyes. In blockchain, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span> plays a much bigger role — it is used to prove ownership, authorize transactions, and secure the entire network.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              The most important cryptographic concept in blockchain is <span class="text-brand-200 font-semibold"><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('asymmetric-crypto')">asymmetric cryptography</span></span>, also known as public-key <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span>. Instead of using a single secret key (like a password), you have two keys: a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> you can share with anyone, and a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> you must keep secret.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              In this chapter, you will learn how public and private keys work, how they are generated, and why they are the foundation of digital ownership in blockchain.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="how-it-works">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">How It Works</h2>

            <div class="mt-4 p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">In public-key <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span>, the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> is derived from the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> using a one-way mathematical function. This means anyone can derive a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> from a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span>, but no one can reverse the process to find the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> from the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span>.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-5 p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-3">Everyday Object Analogy</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Imagine a locked mailbox. Your <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> is the mailbox address — anyone can use it to send you mail. Your <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> is the physical key that unlocks the mailbox. You can give your address to everyone, but only you hold the key to open and read the mail inside.</p>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">How Keys Are Used</h3>
            <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0110 0v4"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200"><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('encryption')">Encryption</span></h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Encrypt data with a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> so only the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> holder can decrypt it.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">Digital Signatures</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Sign data with a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span>. Anyone with the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> can verify the signature.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 1v4m0 14v4m-11-11h4m14 0h4"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">Key Derivation</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Generate a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> from a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> using <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('elliptic-curve')">elliptic curve</span> multiplication.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">Deeper Dive</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              Bitcoin and Ethereum use <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('elliptic-curve')">Elliptic Curve</span> <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">Cryptography</span> (ECC), specifically the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('secp256k1')">secp256k1</span> curve. The math behind ECC makes it easy to compute a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> from a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> but computationally impossible to reverse. This is the foundation of all blockchain security.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              A <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> is a random 256-bit number, roughly equivalent to a number between 1 and 2^256. That is so large that every <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> ever generated is practically guaranteed to be unique. The <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> is a point on the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('elliptic-curve')">elliptic curve</span> derived from this number.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-5 p-4 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-2">Key Insight</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">There are more possible private keys than atoms in the observable universe. You could generate keys until the sun burns out and never produce a duplicate.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="vocabulary">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Vocabulary Table</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="vocab-table w-full text-sm">
                <thead><tr><th class="text-theme">Term</th><th class="text-theme">Definition</th></tr></thead>
                <tbody class="text-theme-muted">
                  <tr id="vocab-cryptography"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">Cryptography</span></td><td>The practice of secure communication through codes and <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('encryption')">encryption</span>.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-public-key"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">Public Key</span></td><td>A cryptographic key that can be shared openly to receive encrypted messages.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-private-key"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">Private Key</span></td><td>A secret cryptographic key that proves ownership and authorizes transactions.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-asymmetric-crypto"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('asymmetric-crypto')">Asymmetric Cryptography</span></td><td>An <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('encryption')">encryption</span> system using paired public and private keys.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-elliptic-curve"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('elliptic-curve')">Elliptic Curve</span></td><td>A mathematical curve used in blockchain cryptography for key generation.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-encryption"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('encryption')">Encryption</span></td><td>Converting readable data into an unreadable format to protect it.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-decryption"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('decryption')">Decryption</span></td><td>Converting encrypted data back into a readable format.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-secp256k1"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('secp256k1')">secp256k1</span></td><td>The specific elliptic curve standard used by Bitcoin and Ethereum.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="fun-facts">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Fun Facts</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg></div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The Caesar cipher, used by Julius Caesar over 2,000 years ago, shifted letters by a fixed number — one of the earliest forms of <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg></div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Public-key <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span> was invented in 1976 by Whitfield Diffie and Martin Hellman, revolutionizing secure communication.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg></div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">A Bitcoin <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> can be represented as a 12- or 24-word seed phrase, making it easier for humans to back up and remember.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg></div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Quantum computers could theoretically break current <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('elliptic-curve')">elliptic curve</span> <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span>, which is why quantum-resistant algorithms are being developed.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3"><svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg></div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The Enigma machine, used by Germany in World War II, was cracked by Alan Turing's Bombe computer — one of history's most famous cryptanalysis achievements.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="interactive-diagram">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8 text-center">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Interactive Diagram</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-theme-muted">Launch the interactive diagram to see this in action.</p>
            <a href="diagrams/diagram-07-digital-signatures/index.html" class="btn-primary magnetic-btn inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm py-3 px-6 mt-4" aria-label="Open interactive diagram">
              Open Interactive Diagram
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="knowledge-check">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Knowledge Check</h2>
            <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">
              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">1. What is a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> used for in blockchain?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> To decrypt messages</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> To receive transactions and verify signatures</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> To mine new blocks</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> To change network rules</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> To receive transactions and verify signatures</p>
              </div>
              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">2. Why can a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> not be derived from a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span>?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> Because the math is one-way and computationally impossible to reverse</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> Because the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('private-key')">private key</span> is stored on a separate server</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> Because the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('public-key')">public key</span> is encrypted</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> Because blockchain networks block reverse lookups</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Because the math is one-way and computationally impossible to reverse</p>
              </div>
              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">3. What curve does Bitcoin use for its <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('cryptography')">cryptography</span>?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> RSA-4096</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('secp256k1')">secp256k1</span></label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> SHA-512</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> AES-256</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('secp256k1')">secp256k1</span></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 text-center">
              <button type="button" id="reveal-answers-btn" class="btn-primary magnetic-btn text-sm py-2.5 px-6">Show Answers</button>
            </div>
            <script>
              (function() { var btn = document.getElementById('reveal-answers-btn'); if (btn) { btn.addEventListener('click', function() { var answers = document.querySelectorAll('.kb-answer'); var hidden = false; answers.forEach(function(a) { if (!a.classList.contains('revealed')) hidden = true; }); answers.forEach(function(a) { a.classList.toggle('revealed', hidden); }); btn.textContent = hidden ? 'Hide Answers' : 'Show Answers'; }); } })();
            </script>
          </div>
        </section>

